The package.json file has two 'dependencies' fields (lines 16-20 and 21-23), which is invalid JSON. The second one overwrites the first in parsers but should be merged into a single dependencies field.

Current:
  "dependencies": {
    "next": "15.3.1",
    "react": "^19.1.0",
    "react-dom": "^19.1.0"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "tailwind-merge": "^6.0.0"
  },

Should be:
  "dependencies": {
    "next": "15.3.1",
    "react": "^19.1.0",
    "react-dom": "^19.1.0",
    "tailwind-merge": "^6.0.0"
  },

File: packages/web/lib/sessions/redaction-utils.ts, function computeCaptureRedactionCounts (modified in staged diff, lines ~253-285).

The staged change now scans the response body when countResponseBody=true and ADDS those counts on top of persistedStats:
  if (persistedStats) {
    const finalByRule = { ...persistedStats.byRule };
    let finalTotal = persistedStats.totalRedactions;
    if (resCounts) {
      for (const [rule, count] of Object.entries(resCounts.byRule)) {
        finalByRule[rule] = (finalByRule[rule] ?? 0) + count;
        finalTotal += count;
      }
    }
    return { totalRedactions: finalTotal, byRule: finalByRule, matches };
  }

Before this change the persistedStats path was authoritative and the response body was never scanned (the param was a no-op '_countResponseBody'). For captures that already carry persisted capture-level redaction stats (produced by the redact plugin, which already includes response-body redactions in totalRedactions/byRule), the new code scans the response body again and ADDS those counts on top — doubling the response portion of every count on every GET.

This affects both packages/web/app/api/captures/[id]/route.ts (computeCaptureRedactionCounts(data, true, redactionStats, ...)) and packages/web/app/api/sessions/[id]/route.ts (per-capture redactionStats), so the displayed 'Redaction Statistics' totals and the per-capture badges are inflated.

Required fix: When persistedStats is provided, treat it as authoritative and do NOT re-add the response-body scan counts (restore prior behavior). Only use the response-body scan path when persistedStats is absent (legacy captures). Do not silently add response-scanned counts to persisted totals.

